{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1509360-how-do-you-go-about-declaring-charms","id":1509360,"title":"How do you go about declaring charms?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-23T04:20:44-07:00","id":1509360,"title":"How do you go about declaring charms?","content":"With system transparency as it is, I had made it the habit, on opposed rolls, to allow PCs and NPCs to go back and forth adding more charms to their pools and more effects to their actions until both sides were satisfied before any rolling took place. I tried to look this up this morning and found that the core book does not say this explicitly. It has some significantly vaguer words on p.216 about knowing what die pools you face. How do you run things?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T04:34:25-07:00","id":1509362,"title":"","content":"Doesn't that trend to mean that everyone essentially gets into a bidding war and blows all their motes in a handful of actions?<br /> <br /> I tend to have the attacker declare dice pools and boosts, and then give the defender a chance to declare be any defence boosts against the now-fixed attack pool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T11:07:38-07:00","id":1509399,"title":"","content":"I also let either side add more in response to the other's declaration. This isn't actually that big of a deal because most NPCs will only have 1 or 2 applicable Charms <i>anyway</i>, so there isn't much back and forth. &quot;The players are tempted to over-commit in response to an enemy&quot; seems fitting for the game.<br /> <br /> Moreover, &quot;the attacker can't double down after hearing the defender declare Charms&quot; gives an enormous advantage to defenders, since they only have to match the offense's investment, while the offense has to wager against how much they <i>think</i> the defender is willing to go, without going so high that the defender just saves all their motes and takes it on the chin to counter-attack instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/396-mr-rage","name":"Mr Rage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T03:53:53-07:00","id":1509942,"title":"","content":"At least by the book, attackers declare before defenders, indicating a single run of Charm declarations each, starting with the attacker. This is from page 251, 2nd paragraph of &quot;Using Charms and Charm Limitations&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","user":"HighPriest","date":". 04-28-2023, 06:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T06:03:10-07:00","id":1509946,"title":"","content":"That's how I do it, but &quot;bidding war&quot; isn't exactly what it turns out in play, because in my experience players will either<br /> &quot;use a couple cheap charms&quot;<br /> &quot;use a couple heavy hitters&quot;<br /> &quot;throw everything they got&quot;<br /> <br /> So long I keep the same paradigm for the npcs, the usual banter is &quot;NPC is doing this with this many dice, this extra trick and a rider effect on hit&quot; vs &quot;ok i'm replying with this much excellency and these two charms&quot;. One declaration each.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}